build/
# Inputs, not outputs: hand-fetched or separately built, and NOT
# reproducible by make. Kept out of build/ precisely so `make clean`
# (rm -rf build/) cannot destroy them -- it did, once, silently
# disarming seven test binaries (#191).
build-inputs/
core
core.*
image/keys/*.key
.claude/
backups/

# Real, recipe-built package artifacts fetched for the test floor
# (ADR-0209). Not committed: they are large binaries whose one source
# of truth is the artifact cache plus the checksum in each recipe --
# committing copies would be a second place the same bytes live.
#
# ANYWHERE in the tree, not only under build-inputs/: `cixctl pkg
# artifact-export` writes into the current directory, and on
# 2026-09-27 a libmnl export made at the repository root was swept into
# a CHANGELOG commit (a937ee32) by `git add -A`. This paragraph existed
# then, with no pattern under it to enforce it.
*.cixpkg
*.cixpkg.minisig

# Generated by tools/apigen.c from docs/api/openapi.yaml on every build
# (ADR-0218). It lives here rather than under build/ only because the
# dashboard SERVES it; like every other generated artifact it is never
# committed, and the one editable source is the spec.
web/api.js
